
import java.util.* ;
import java.io.*; 
public class Solution {

	public static int findKthElement(int[][] matrix, int k) {
	    // Write your code here.
		int n = matrix.length;
		int m = matrix[0].length;
		int top = 0;
		int left = 0;
		int bottom = n-1;
		int right = m-1;
		int cnt = 0;
		

		while(top <= bottom && left <= right){
			for(int i = left; i <= right; i++){
				cnt++;
				if(cnt == k) return matrix[top][i];
				
			}
			top++;

			for(int j = top; j <= bottom; j++){
				cnt++;
				if(cnt == k) return matrix[j][right];
			}
			right--;

			if(top <= bottom){
				for(int i = right; i >= left; i--){
					cnt++;
					if(cnt == k) return matrix[bottom][i];

				}
				bottom--;
			}

			if(left <= right){
				for(int i = bottom; i >= top; i--){
					cnt++;
					if(cnt == k) return matrix[i][left];
				}
				left++;
			}
		}
		return -1;

		
	}
}



Problem statement
Given a matrix with ‘N’ rows and ‘M’ columns and an integer ‘K’. Your task is to find the “Kth” element which is obtained while traversing the matrix in spiral form.

Spiral Traversing in the matrix:

The below picture can clearly show how to traverse a matrix in spiral form.
mat = [
  [1,  2,  3],
  [4,  5,  6],
  [7,  8,  9]
]
Spiral order →
1, 2, 3, 6, 9, 8, 7, 4, 5

Let’s pick:
👉 k = 5

Steps to traverse the array :-
We maintain boundaries:

top = 0

bottom = n - 1

left = 0

right = m - 1

And a counter cnt to track how many elements have been visited.

Count	Element
1	     1
2      2
3	     3
4    	 6
5   	 9

✅ Answer = 9

*******At each step:********

Traverse left → right (top row)

Traverse top+1 → bottom (right column)

Traverse right-1 → left (bottom row) — only if rows remain

Traverse bottom-1 → top+1 (left column) — only if columns remain

Whenever cnt == k, return that element.

T.C => O(N * M)
S.C => O(1)
